WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.794 --> 00:00:05.380
The next day Lissa sat with Jason in front of her computer. "The judges said to

2
00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:13.795
bring a recipe to the contest," she murmured. "I need to find something that will

3
00:00:13.796 --> 00:00:17.716
really impress them." "You make delicious burnt chocolate chunk cookies." Lissa grinned. "I thought you said

4
00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:24.610
you were going to help me, not insult me!" Jason turned back to the screen. "What

5
00:00:24.611 --> 00:00:31.602
about this recipe for chocolate caramel cake?" "Our recipe needs to have fruit or vegetables

6
00:00:31.603 --> 00:00:36.778
in it," she reminded him. "I can make that cake for your bake sale though." "As

7
00:00:36.779 --> 00:00:40.008
long as I get to taste it first." Jason scrolled downward. "So . . .

8
00:00:40.009 --> 00:00:46.933
we need something with fruit or vegetables." He wrinkled his nose. "Who would put vegetables in

9
00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:57.923
a dessert?" "Well, lots of people like carrot cake," Lissa said. "And sweet potato pie." "Right."

10
00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:04.590
Jason nodded. "My mom bakes zucchini bread sometimes." "Yuck." Lissa made a face. "First of

11
00:01:04.591 --> 00:01:11.080
all, zucchini is disgusting. And second of all, it's technically a fruit, not a vegetable." "Okay,

12
00:01:11.081 --> 00:01:22.636
so no zucchini recipes!" Jason paused to look at an image of a banana cream pie.

13
00:01:22.637 --> 00:01:33.638
"What about this?" Lissa skimmed the ingredients. "This could work." "Great." Jason leaped to his

14
00:01:33.639 --> 00:01:38.047
feet. "Let's start baking!" *** So began another week of cooking. Every day Lissa tried a

15
00:01:38.048 --> 00:01:44.555
new recipe. Sometimes Jason helped by cracking eggs or creaming butter and sugar together. Other times

16
00:01:44.556 --> 00:01:50.628
he just tasted the results. He wasn't a very critical judge, as Lissa had already

17
00:01:50.629 --> 00:01:59.040
seen from his enjoyment of her burnt cookies. But he was very encouraging. "Delicious!" he said

18
00:01:59.041 --> 00:02:09.187
again and again. "Another winner!" The two of them worked their way through recipes for

19
00:02:09.188 --> 00:02:14.687
banana cream pie, a cherry crisp, rhubarb custard bars, and raspberry crumb cake. Dad shook his

20
00:02:14.688 --> 00:02:24.575
head every time he entered the busy kitchen. "I've gained ten pounds since this competition started!"

21
00:02:24.576 --> 00:02:35.321
"It's your fault," Lissa told him. "You're the one who made me sign up!" While

22
00:02:35.322 --> 00:02:42.004
Jason and Lissa experimented with recipes for the contest, they also talked about the bake sale

23
00:02:42.005 --> 00:02:50.472
for the community center. Jason was still figuring out the details. Meanwhile, Lissa was thinking about

24
00:02:50.473 --> 00:03:01.314
desserts to bake for it, starting with that chocolate caramel cake. On Thursday, Lissa made

25
00:03:01.315 --> 00:03:12.390
a batch of peach hand pies. While the small pies were cooling, she reviewed her ideas

26
00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:19.964
for the next round of the cooking competition. "I've got one more day to practice

27
00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:30.613
recipes," she thought. "I'll make up my mind about a recipe tomorrow." When the hand pies

28
00:03:30.614 --> 00:03:40.305
were cool, she put some on a tray and headed outside, where Jason was playing basketball.

29
00:03:40.306 --> 00:03:47.541
Abruptly, she froze. Rob and Kelly were walking up Jason's driveway. Lissa took a step

30
00:03:47.542 --> 00:03:52.599
backward. Jason stopped playing basketball and waved to his friends. Then he caught sight of Lissa.

31
00:03:52.600 --> 00:04:02.602
"Yes! It's snack time! Bring those treats out here, Lissa!" Lissa took a deep breath and

32
00:04:02.603 --> 00:04:10.605
approached the other kids. Jason was grinning happily at everyone. "So do you two know

33
00:04:10.606 --> 00:04:17.256
what recipes you're going to bake on Saturday? Lissa's been trying all sorts of things." He

34
00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:20.423
looked at the tray. "What have you got today?" "Peach hand pies," Lissa said. "Huh? Hand

35
00:04:20.424 --> 00:04:29.083
pies?" Kelly frowned as she peered at the small fruit pies. "Aren't they called turnovers?"

36
00:04:29.084 --> 00:04:33.821
Lissa shrugged. "I've always called them hand pies." "Who cares what they're called?" Jason reached for

37
00:04:33.822 --> 00:04:47.414
one and bit in. "Perfect!" he declared, wiping warm peach juice from his chin. Rob

38
00:04:47.415 --> 00:04:53.161
tried one too, and his eyebrows went up. "These taste awesome!" "I know," Lissa replied. "I've

39
00:04:53.162 --> 00:05:03.723
been baking them for years." She no longer cared if the other kids thought she was

40
00:05:03.724 --> 00:05:09.786
a show-off. At least she was honest. Rob cocked an eye at her. "Maybe I'll

41
00:05:09.787 --> 00:05:16.204
hire you to bake pies for my diner someday." Kelly had taken one from the tray

42
00:05:16.205 --> 00:05:25.949
too. "These are good," she said. "Thanks." Lissa looked away. Suddenly she had a panicky thought.

43
00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:33.522
Kelly and Rob were her competitors in the cooking contest. Maybe she should be keeping

44
00:05:33.523 --> 00:05:40.357
her recipes secret. What if Kelly and Rob decided to make hand pies too? Quickly Lissa

45
00:05:40.358 --> 00:05:48.513
changed the subject. "So, Jason, is there anything new with the bake sale?" He shook his

46
00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:53.769
head. "I still need to find a place where we can have it. I could

47
00:05:53.770 --> 00:06:05.916
just hold it here at my house, I guess." "What bake sale?" Rob asked. "Hey, Jason!"

48
00:06:05.917 --> 00:06:11.170
Just then Mia appeared. She tossed her long, silky hair and smiled widely at Jason,

49
00:06:11.171 --> 00:06:15.243
barely looking at anybody else. Lissa saw Kelly roll her eyes. "Hmm," Lissa thought. "Maybe I'm

50
00:06:15.244 --> 00:06:18.838
not the only one who finds Mia annoying." "What are you doing, Jason?" Mia asked. Jason

51
00:06:18.839 --> 00:06:23.982
explained about the bake sale to raise money for the new community center. "Our city

52
00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:30.475
needs more basketball courts. And stuff for kids to do in the summertime." Mia's eyes flicked

53
00:06:30.476 --> 00:06:35.549
to Lissa. "You've been planning this with her ?" "Yep." Rob looked thoughtful. "Jason, I think

54
00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:45.144
you could make it a really big event. Then you could raise lots of money."

55
00:06:45.145 --> 00:06:47.978
"What do you mean?" Jason asked. "You need to spread the word about the bake sale

56
00:06:47.979 --> 00:06:55.630
so it's not just a bunch of your friends and neighbors buying stuff," Rob said.

57
00:06:55.631 --> 00:07:04.029
Kelly's eyes lit up. "I know! You could have the bake sale at the Garden, after

58
00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:08.775
the last round of the cooking competition. There would already be a lot of people there

59
00:07:08.776 --> 00:07:14.180
because of the competition. And I bet Betty would love the idea. It would attract

60
00:07:14.181 --> 00:07:20.704
lots of new customers." "That's a good idea, Kelly!" Jason looked at Lissa. "Why didn't we

61
00:07:20.705 --> 00:07:27.084
think of that?" Lissa shrugged, unsure of what to say. The other kids had lived here

62
00:07:27.085 --> 00:07:32.330
longer than she had. Plus, maybe they were just smarter or more creative than she

63
00:07:32.331 --> 00:07:38.173
was. "I'll talk to my dad," Rob said. "He knows a lot about fundraising. I bet

64
00:07:38.174 --> 00:07:43.498
he can even help us set up a fund so that people can donate online." "You

65
00:07:43.499 --> 00:07:48.513
definitely need to get a story in the newspaper," Mia added. "My uncle is a

66
00:07:48.514 --> 00:07:53.581
reporter. I'll tell him about the bake sale." "Wow." Jason looked happy—even happier than usual. "This

67
00:07:53.582 --> 00:08:02.479
sounds great. Thanks, you guys!" Lissa was glad for Jason, but she couldn't help feeling

68
00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:09.989
a little bad as the kids kept talking about their ideas. The bake sale had seemed

69
00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:16.565
fun when it was just her and Jason doing the planning. But now . . .

70
00:08:16.566 --> 00:08:25.797
Abruptly, Lissa grabbed her tray. "See you later," she said. "I've got a bunch of

71
00:08:25.798 --> 00:08:33.433
other recipes to try." As she hurried home, none of the others bothered to say good-bye.

